window.docContents[66].resolve({"/Appendix/#section-chapter-5-maps-results":{"contents":"* isRegular_of_isVertexTransitive: a locally finite vertex-transitive graph is\nregular.* isVertexTransitive_top: the complete graph is vertex-transitive.* isVertexTransitive_cycleGraph: the cycle graph C[n] is vertex-transitive.* isVertexTransitive_hypercube: the hypercube Q[n] is vertex-transitive.* isVertexTransitive_mycielskian_iff: for finite nonempty V, the Mycielskian\nmμ[G] is vertex-transitive iff G ≃g K[2].* degree_tensorProd: the degree of (v, w) in the tensor product is\nG.degree v * H.degree w.* clawFree_lineGraph: line graphs are claw-free.* top_three_isContained_lineGraph_iff: the line graph of G contains a triangle\niff G contains a triangle or a (not necessarily induced) copy of the claw.\n\nFrom the exercises:\n\n* IsVertexTransitive.compl / isVertexTransitive_bot: the complement of a\nvertex-transitive graph is vertex-transitive, so ⊥ is vertex-transitive.\n\n","context":"Graph Theory in Lean\u0009Appendix\u0009Results","header":"14.3.3. Chapter 5: Maps (Results)","id":"/Appendix/#section-chapter-5-maps-results"}});